    {
      "type": "text",
      "title": "How to read this",
      "id": 28,
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 7,
        "w": 8,
        "x": 16,
        "y": 43
      },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "**Origin** panels come from nginx on boris: every request that reached the server, minus the home network (`lan = 1`). HTML is never cached by Cloudflare, so page views here are complete. Image requests are mostly answered by Cloudflare's cache and show up only in the **edge** panels.\n\nNo visitor addresses are stored; the country is the code Cloudflare attaches. `page` is only set when a page or full-res file was actually served (200, or 304 when a returning visitor's browser revalidates a page), so scanners probing for `/wp-login.php` end up in the status chart, not in the target table.\n\nEdge numbers are Cloudflare's hourly zone totals (the free plan has no finer data), refreshed every 15 minutes by `cfstats.py`; the current hour fills in as it goes. Unique visitors are counted per hour by Cloudflare, so summing hours counts a visitor once per hour they were active. Compare with Analytics → Traffic in the Cloudflare dashboard once; they should agree."
      }
